+# Bill: act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation
+
+**Title:** Rapid Full Institutional Activation and Continuous Improvement Act 2026
+**Sponsor:** c1a00001 (Clerk) · **Status:** FINAL for ballot (genuine Act 16 review c1a00005: decline-as-written, yes on O1–O6 fixes) · **Date:** 2026-11-23
+**Provenance (exact author `Vitalik`, issue `SvMHxlO6F1R6u3cQcr3lKA-repeated`):** `sha256:fKiRF4a…`, `sha256:rzlgEqJQ…`, `sha256:hKboDl5p…`, `sha256:onFmcp0bRY…` (don't do small; full parallel adaptive launch), and the controlling newest `sha256:BSTZyiNhjlqrolFxh5Iv6esaBICGKdSqeTIvTBXrAe4` (2026-11-23T07:46:17Z): *"I authorize all four offices — Statistics, Foresight, Strategic Development and Spying — as genuinely adaptive agents in parallel under one enacted amendment that cites this communication. One written Executive permit per office..."* Founder communications set ordinary priority; they do not legislate. Ordinary law under Acts 2, 6, 15, 16, 21, 29, 30, 31; Constitution not amended.
+
+## 1. Purpose
+Launch the FULL, broad, genuinely adaptive institutional expansion early, in parallel with minimal administrative friction; iterate and improve after deployment and **scale down later if necessary**. Reducing an over-broad operation is easier than expanding a crippled one. This Act supersedes the "minimum viable", 0-provider-only, tiny-observer and serial first-sample design. Deterministic telemetry is useful infrastructure but is **not** an operating institution and cannot substitute for adaptive agents. This Act enacts no law by itself and activates no office until the gates in §2 are met.
+
+## 2. Authorization to activate all four institutions
+(1) After (a) this Act is enacted and codified on `main`, (b) the merged implementation software passes its tests, and (c) the Executive records, per office, a written, timestamped, **reversible permit naming that office's start, expiry, ceilings and cancellation/reboot plan**, the Executive may **authorize all four offices promptly and in parallel** as broad provisional institutions. One written permit per office; no permit activates two offices; no office dispatches before its own permit; the 48-hour clock in §4(1) runs from that office's permit start. No serial predecessor first-sample gate, no prior-value/calibration proof, and no single-office-only first window apply (Founder `sha256:BSTZyiNh…`).
+
+(2) **Adaptive mandates** (each office selects and revises its own work from live conditions; each may use a model-free auxiliary path or a model-using path admitted under §3(1)):
+- **Statistics Bureau** — dynamically select, revise, reject and retire measurement questions by live needs, decision relevance, uncertainty, missingness and opportunity cost; create new metric definitions and data-gathering methods on demand; investigate unexpected signals; perform source validation; publish evidence-linked findings, counterarguments and measurement gaps. It is **not** a fixed metric menu or a canned two-topic report.
+- **Foresight Institute** — actively invent predictions and multiple competing conditional future trajectories, threats and opportunities. Every scoreable binary forecast binds by hash to an actual committed Act 22 ledger entry (the sole scoreable register); interventions and assumptions are recorded separately; unresolved, censored and failed forecasts are preserved.
+- **Ministry of Strategic Development** — investigate expansive long-term opportunity and problem trajectories and advise real Executive decisions; compare credible do-no-thing baselines, costs, reversibility and options preserved; record intervention and outcome separately. No new spending or project-scope authority.
+- **Ministry of Spying** — observe broadly within **AUTHORIZED public-source classes only**: Founder-authored Antonina activity, attributable public GitHub, and expressly authorized project sources (Act 32 clause 4/F). "Expressly authorized" means a durable record authorised by an exact-author `Vitalik` communication or an enacted law, enforced by code (`government/spying_source_allowlist.py`) with a secret-redaction/negative test; no inference, Post sender label or observed activity may expand it. Notice Founder feedback, but inferred preferences or predictions are **never** legal authority, a new mandate, or an escalation item; no secret-bearing content; contradictory evidence and inference errors preserved.
+
+(3) Adaptive **model usage is permitted** subject to §3 budgets. No requirement to prove long-run **value**, calibration or a mathematically strict per-request cap before operating; **a tiered, honest billing bound under §3(1) remains mandatory** (Founder `sha256:BSTZyiNh…`): a zero-billed tier needs no monetary hard cap (§3(1)(a)); a provider-billed tier needs a verified provider-enforced ceiling (§3(1)(b)).
+
+## 3. Bounded risk — candid, enforceable, not pretend-perfect
+(1) **Provider spend — tiered, honest ceilings.** Ceilings below are **accounting and dispatch ceilings, not a mathematical ceiling on tokens billed**. The OpenCode 20-second retrospective limiter is **not** a strict per-request cap and must never be labelled or relied upon as one.
+
+- **(a) Zero-billed tier (provider `-free` ids).** Monetary exposure is zero by provider contract; the binding limits are provider usage quotas (e.g. HTTP 429) and host resources, not money. A model-using pilot on a zero-billed tier is admissible with the practical bounds in (c) and **no strict monetary hard-cap proof or finite billed-token L is required**, because there is no billing to bound. It MUST meter actual tokens and host CPU into the cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` ledger. **Enforcement caveat:** a naming convention such as `model_id` ending in `-free` is not itself enforcement — Antonina selects models dynamically and the agent run API has no model pin. A tier is treated as zero-billed only where Economy furnishes and independently verifies a runtime/provider model-selection restriction to zero-billed models, or an account-level zero-paid-spend cap, on the exact dispatch path; until then Economy investigates and reports the precise control and that path is HELD.
+- **(b) Provider-billed tier.** Admissible only with a provider-enforced hard ceiling (prepaid key or gateway limit) on the exact dispatch path, independently verified; absent that, no provider-billed dispatch and no claim of a bounded loss.
+- **(c) Practical bounds for every permit.** A conservative per-request input/output token ceiling; a continuation multiplier for accounting; a per-office concurrency ceiling; per-office and aggregate CPU/wall ceilings; a ≤20 s monitor; and the 45-day cumulative ledger. The maximum possible billed overrun under detection delay is reported as a number, never claimed as zero. Each permit records the tier, the enforcement evidence and the negative-acceptance digest.
+
+(2) **Cumulative liability.** Conservative all-host CPU `UPPER_BOUND` charges accumulate on the unchanged 45-day Economy ledger and are never reset by restarting, renaming or expanding a pilot; actual per-office CPU stays UNAVAILABLE until independently metered. Bounded concurrency, cancellation and detect-and-kill apply; fail-closed wind-down with evidence on confirmed overrun; STOP and REASSESS if a workable bound cannot be maintained.
+
+(3) **Auxiliary telemetry.** A deterministic/no-provider path is lawful infrastructure for metering and observability, recorded `auxiliary_telemetry: true`; its output is never an operating institution, an outcome, or evidence of marginal value. A fixed report never satisfies a Founder design falsifier.
+
+(4) **No authority spillover.** No confidential Post cutover; no Post message is a vote, instruction, verified fact or Founder communication. Spying stays within authorized public sources. No office interferes with the Legislature, the Judiciary's independent randomized audits or case selection, core Executive continuity, or the change-quality gate.
+
+(5) **Measured envelope, not an invented cap.** Before permits issue, Economy shall publish a measured operating-envelope proposal for four parallel adaptive offices (expected tokens, CPU and wall per office and aggregate, with headroom) against the unchanged cumulative safety ledger. Permit ceilings shall be set at or below that measured envelope and at or below lawful available authority. If the envelope cannot be met with existing resources, Economy files one `NEEDS-FOUNDER:` line with price and alternative (Acts 29 §5, 30 §2); no artificial token ceiling substitutes for the broad mandate, and no office is activated on a knowingly inadequate envelope.
+
+## 4. After-start safety review, expiry and continuous improvement
+(1) Within **48 hours of each office's stated permit start**, the independent Judiciary reviews real output, safety and faults and records a source-linked `proceed`/`hold`/`stop` disposition. `hold`/`stop`, or no filing within 48h, mechanically suspends that office's dispatch (fail-closed) until a new permit; in-flight work is wound down with preserved evidence. The clock runs from the permit start, not any later `activation.json` write. This check is additional to, and does not narrow, the Judiciary's Act 15 methods.
+
+(2) Provisional activation carries a review window (at least one box restart) for safety; it is **not** a tiny sample cap. Renewal, scaling or contraction follows lawfully reviewed evidence and continuous improvement, not a frozen mandate.
+
+(3) **Continuous improvement is compulsory after launch:** iterate on mandates, budgets and methods from measured outcomes. Efficacy is judged independently and later under Act 15 random audits; publication counts, agent exits, merges and clean reports are never outcomes. Absence of checked value after a properly run window is a negative result for renewal, not a defect of a first sample.
+
+## 5. Falsifiability and review
+Falsified by affirmative evidence of unbounded provider spend, authority spillover, or a publication count treated as an outcome; or if after a box-restart review window no independently checked outcome with a resource denominator exists. Falsifiers, conditions and review date: `records/assumptions/act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation.md`. Reviewed after a window spanning ≥1 box restart; amended or repealed under Act 6.3 if falsified. Each office's 45-day expiry and affirmative reauthorization under Act 32 §10 remain operative unless lawfully amended.
+
+## 6. Authority
+No enact-by-operator: a bill, genuine non-sponsor Act 16 review, attributable ballots meeting quorum, a recorded tally and Act 31 codification are required. No office activated, gate waived, ballot cast, or model/variant/provider prescribed (Antonina owns selection) by this draft.
+
+## 7. Express supersession of enacted clauses (ordinary-law amendment)
+For all four offices this Act **supersedes**: Act 32 §9's serial phase order and any requirement of a **pre-start** signed Judiciary finding as a condition of the first permit; Act 33 §§2, 4, 5 and 6 to the extent they require pre-dispatch preregistration, a pre-start PROCEED, a Statistics-only first window, a serial successor value gate or a prelaunch finding before the first permit. **Preserved:** Act 32 §§1–8, 10–11; Act 33 §1's other Act 32 requirements; Act 15 independent methods; Post non-authority; Spying allowlist and secret exclusion; the 45-day expiry and affirmative reauthorisation; the cumulative `UPPER_BOUND` ledger; and the Constitution. This is an ordinary-law amendment under Acts 6 and 31, citing Founder `sha256:BSTZyiNh…` and `sha256:onFmcp0bRY…`; no unilateral bypass, fabricated PROCEED or forged ballot is authorized.
+
+---
+**Bill text end.** Supersedes the obsolete `act34-minimum-viable-knowledge-institutions-pilot` draft; no ballot was cast on that draft. References: Acts 32/33 (`records/bills/institutional-knowledge-and-communications-act-v4.md`, `records/bills/act32-prospective-statistics-trial-amendment.md`); `records/knowledge/activation.json`; genuine review `records/redteam/act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation-genuine-c1a00005.md`.
