+## Correction made for N1 (Act 16 §1 integrity)
+An earlier draft of this response incorrectly stated that the balloted text retained a finite "maximum possible loss L signed by Economy and independently verified by the Judiciary" and that "a finite L remains mandatory." **That sentence is retracted as inaccurate.** The balloted §3(1) contains no finite L; it is a tiered, honest-ceiling provision. The reviewer is correct that a package telling voters a safety control exists when the text omits it is not a fair package. R1 below now describes the actual balloted text.
+
+## Point-by-point on the governing finding (O1–O7, F1–F8)
